 "overview": "The MPS School Committee is the governing body for the Medford Public Schools district, responsible for setting district policy, overseeing school operations, approving annual budgets, supervising district leadership, and managing collective bargaining and capital infrastructure projects. The committee's archive spans meetings from April 2022 through October 2026, across the 2022–2023, 2024–2025, and 2026–2027 terms. Key recurring focus areas include advancing a comprehensive high school building project through the Massachusetts School Building Authority (MSBA) process, executing multi-million-dollar HVAC and building renovations across district schools, expanding before and after school capacity, and settling labor agreements across all operational units. The body also managed superintendent leadership transitions and responded to elementary school space constraints and overcrowding. At its most recent meeting, the committee selected a ground-source geothermal HVAC system for Missituk Elementary, approved a Construction Manager at Risk delivery method for Roberts Elementary, and reviewed a first-quarter financial update.",
