  {
   "name": "Medford High School MSBA Building Project",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "The committee authorized initial Statements of Interest to the Massachusetts School Building Authority core program for Medford High School in 2022 to address substantial energy, accessibility, and infrastructure deficiencies [M01#3, M03#1]. After re-submitting applications, the district was invited into the MSBA eligibility phase in late 2023 [M21#7, M28#6, M47#5]. The committee formally established the Medford Comprehensive High School Building Committee, defining its governance, membership, and educational goals [M51#5, M52#2, M57#8]. Transitioning into feasibility studies, the committee hired Left Field as Owner's Project Manager, selected design consultants, and finalized an enrollment capacity agreement with the MSBA [M89#4, M96#5, M112#5, M113#3]. Facing site constraints such as a Department of Conservation and Recreation deed restriction on Edgerly Field, the committee narrowed design alternatives and continued community engagement forums into 2026 [M122#3, M125#2, M128#4, M130#7].",
