   "name": "Collective Bargaining and Union Negotiations",
   "status": "settled",
   "summary": "The committee managed labor relations and contract renewals for bargaining units representing teachers, administrators, paraprofessionals, custodians, nurses, cafeteria workers, and administrative secretaries. Following a formal impasse declaration and state mediation with the Medford Teachers Association in 2022, the body ratified successive multi-year agreements with educators [M05#7, M10#5, M14#4, M20#5, M95#3]. Contracts were regularly negotiated and approved for administrators [M41#1, M53#4, M98#6, M100#7], custodians and secretaries [M65#2], cafeteria workers [M64#2], paraprofessionals and Kids Corner staff [M13#2, M68#2, M68#3, M102#2], and school nurses [M11#1, M104#1]. Executive sessions were routinely convened to manage bargaining strategy across all employment classifications [M18#1, M38#2, M80#1, M126#2].",
