  {
   "name": "School Facilities Infrastructure and HVAC Upgrades",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "District-wide cooling failures and aging building infrastructure led the committee to initiate comprehensive capital facility reviews in late 2023 [M39#6]. The committee approved a $15 to $20 million partial-decarbonization HVAC scope for Andrews and McGlynn middle schools [M59#6], authorized Construction Management at Risk procurement [M80#6], and approved $5 million and $25.7 million project bonding requests [M84#6, M93#7]. A district-wide facility condition assessment identified $83.7 million in prioritized repairs across five schools [M107#3]. The committee also submitted MSBA Accelerated Repair applications [M91#1], approved a $22.7 million schematic design for HVAC and roof work at Roberts Elementary [M133#4], and selected a ground-source geothermal HVAC system for Missituk Elementary [M137#4].",
