   "name": "Elementary School Overcrowding and Space Planning",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "Severe overcrowding at Roberts Elementary School prompted the committee to evaluate space utilization and enrollment distribution across elementary facilities [M70#8, M71#6]. The committee formed a task force, requested administrative enrollment reports, and referred overcrowding solutions to subcommittees [M94#4, M99#7]. To relieve space constraints at Roberts Elementary, the committee authorized moving Medford Early Education Program (MEEP) preschool classrooms to Missituk Elementary [M99#6]. The committee also studied broader middle school grade reconfiguration models—such as shifting to K–4, 5–6, and 7–8 grade spans—and gathered community feedback [M108#5, M109#5], before voting to delay any middle school grade configuration changes to the 2028–2029 school year [M132#4].",
