  {
   "name": "Before and After School Programming Expansion",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "Persistent waitlists and staffing shortages in elementary after-school programs led the committee to replace waitlists with lotteries and adjust tuition and staff pay rates [M11#7, M19#4, M26#5, M28#8, M53#7]. The committee requested regular administrative reporting on waitlists and expanded provider partnerships [M75#8, M80#3]. In 2025, the body contracted the Belmont Afterschool Enrichment Collaborative (BASIC) for a comprehensive program evaluation [M97#2], introduced an early pickup fee option [M100#5], and transitioned site coordinators to full-time status [M102#3]. Adopting BASIC recommendations, the committee approved an expanded programming structure adding 150 seats, full-time directors, and updated rate cards, achieving a 50 percent enrollment increase and reduced waitlists [M123#4, M123#5, M137#3].",
